This page describes the planned `Paleontology` catalog format. Once released,
specimens in a project using this format will show the fossil attribute form.
Weight units and sex work the same way across taxon groups; see
[Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

{% aside type="danger" %}

Paleontology support is in development and is not yet available in released
versions of NAHPU. Track progress in the
[`dev` branch](https://github.com/nahpu/nahpu/tree/dev). Fields and this page
may change before release.

{% /aside %}

## Fossil attributes

- `Fossil type`: kind of fossil, such as a body fossil or trace fossil.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex controlled vocabulary.
- `Ontogenetic stage`: developmental stage of the individual.
- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `Specimen description`: free-text description of the specimen.
- `Remarks`: additional notes.

## Sites

Paleontology projects replace the site habitat form with sedimentology fields:
`Depositional Environment Type`, `Depositional Environment Subtype`,
`Standard Preservation Type`, `Rock Type(s)`, and
`Comments on sedimentology and paleoenvironment`. Choose a continental or marine
environment type before selecting its subtype. See
[Sites](/en/usages/sites/).
